@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+## Context
+
+`createRentalService` in `src/index.ts` keeps equipment in a `Map` and bookings in an array with `startMs`/`endMs`. `book` already validates periods via `parseInstant` and tests overlap on half-open intervals.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Reuse `parseInstant` and the same overlap predicate (`b.start < end && start < b.end`) so availability and `book` can never disagree. Extract the period validation and the overlap test into small helpers shared by `price`, `book` and `availability`.
+- Filter equipment by `kind` when given, exclude any item with an overlapping booking, and sort ids with the default string comparison (`Array.prototype.sort()` on ids), giving a deterministic order.
+- An invalid `kind` throws, consistent with `addEquipment`, rather than silently returning an empty list (assumption recorded here).
+- Add an `AvailabilityQuery` interface and the method to `RentalService`.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Linear scan over bookings per item: fine at the size of a school's stock.
